FILED s543p (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-27, CODE 0ab08642 = MAIN-READY-111, v2-16300) by the Rosetta census (docs/rosetta-plan.md step 1; #2104).

THE SHAPE (neutral reproducer, run on the tree, perl 5.40.3 vs PCL):

    my $s = "aab"; pos($s) = 0;
    my @l = $s =~ /\Ga/gc;
    print pos($s) // 'undef', "\n";     # perl 2      PCL undef
    pos($s) = 1;
    @l = $s =~ /\Gq/gc;
    print pos($s) // 'undef', "\n";     # perl 1      PCL undef
    pos($s) = 1;
    @l = $s =~ /q/gc;
    print pos($s) // 'undef', "\n";     # perl 1      PCL 1   (the unanchored arm is right, #2001)

WHERE: cl/pcl-runtime.lisp `do-regex-match`, the first `cond` arm ("/\G.../g in list context"): it ends in an unconditional `(remhash string *p-match-pos*)`; the unanchored list arm below it tests `cont-p` and records the last match's end through `%p-set-match-pos` (#2001's two lines).  The anchored arm needs the same `cont-p` test (and, on a miss with /c, to leave pos alone).

Found while reducing 0071, where it is the visible half of #5460 (with #5460 fixed that program's match is void, i.e. scalar, and this arm is not reached).


=== DONE (s543u) ===
The anchored list \G//g arm keeps pos under /c at the last match's end, or where it was on a miss (the unanchored arm's #2001 rule); %pcl-scan-anchored-list returns the last start and end.  The task's three rows are p2-gpos rows 24-26: perl = tree.  Guard row 74.  0071 is same with it (its visible half).
